{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "moss",
      "decision": "develop",
      "ability": null,
      "reason": "The implemented scratch comparison establishes specimen-specific relative resistance, not the absolute threshold required by the other tools. Neither the branch comparison nor a load test supplies an independent absolute reference. Develop a small, instrumented contact-response protocol that attempts to identify the threshold from measured force, geometry and permanent surface change under the actual physical law. Its executable precursor is a paid contact-response sweep; certification must remain unresolved if the physical law cannot support an independently anchored inversion.",
      "specification": "Implement contact-resistance-calibration v1 through the current handoff. Separate code reuse of hardness-assessment's specimen resolver, contact mechanics, debris conservation and surface inspection from this new absolute-measurement function. Public schema: {mode: 'inspect'|'sweep'|'assess'|'resume'|'cancel', target: string, counterface: string, project: string}; require all fields, reject extra properties, allow empty unused references. Shared reference semantics: target and counterface resolve explicit owned item IDs, never silently substitute resource types; project resolves an actor-owned persistent project. Dependencies: personal hardness-assessment mastery; actual distinct solid specimens with inspected usable surfaces; a versioned measurement model grounded in the world's existing contact mechanics. No reference stock, apparatus or certified specimen is created by implementation.\nBefore enabling absolute assessment, audit the existing contact law and publish its observable forward model, dimensional anchors, index mapping, uncertainty and identifiability limits. Force and pressure already recorded by the scratch handler may be used only where those records represent actual measured contact quantities; do not expose intrinsic material indices as readings. Never change material properties or redefine the >=8 predicate to make calibration succeed. If the model lacks independent anchors or has indistinguishable responses across the threshold, implement the sweep and an explicit unresolved result identifying the missing physical standard or measurement dependency; do not manufacture calibration lineage.\nInspect costs one round and 0.2 energy. Sweep reserves 0.1 unit from each specimen and performs four directional contacts, one per round at 0.5 energy, followed by one inspection round at 0.2 energy. Use two actual usable contact geometries and two measured force levels within the existing safe contact envelope; record achieved rather than merely requested values. Geometry that cannot be obtained from the supplied specimens produces an insufficient-geometry result, not a free prepared edge. Persist contact area/radius, force, pressure, dwell, grooves, transfer, wear, fracture, debris and uncertainty. Each contact executes existing physical mechanics and conserves all detached material. No contact may certify through resource names or comparison ranking alone. Assess costs one round and 0.2 energy and computes the full index interval compatible with all observations and the independently anchored model. Report supported >=8 only if the conservative lower bound is >=8, below-threshold only if its upper bound is <8, otherwise unresolved. A model with no finite supported bound returns null bounds. Results apply only to the tested material extent; do not certify its parent stack without independently supported homogeneity.\nState includes model version and anchor provenance, resolved specimen IDs, escrow owner, allocations, completed stages, actual remaining work, paid costs, observations and certificate validity. Missing energy pauses without charge. Action change, loss of reach, specimen destruction or death cancels active work once, releasing surviving unconsumed escrow to its owner or the ground at the actual location if dead; altered specimens and debris remain altered, with no cloning, deletion or refund. Resume explicitly reacquires the same surviving project materials and performs only remaining stages. Global pauses preserve progress. Completion requires every paid stage and the final assessment; cancellation never implies completion.\nUse shared collision and interaction geometry: contacts require both actual surfaces within 0.65 reach, with no remote contact or overlapping placement. Certificates persist surface identity, wear and model lineage; subsequent damage, contamination or unsupported transfer invalidates applicability. Existing tool consumers may accept a valid conservative certificate for the tested item only while retaining their actual intrinsic >=8 checks. Migrate old comparisons unchanged as relative-only evidence, with null absolute bounds and no retroactive certification. Declare contact-calibration-progress, contact-calibration-completed, contact-calibration-stopped and contact-calibration-invalidated events, and validate subscriptions to existing information-confirmed. Implementation and review advance no simulation time and grant neither mastery nor materials.",
      "experienceReview": "An actual experiment resolving previously unknown absolute bounds—or establishing a previously unknown, measured limitation of the method—can benefit this actor through grounded understanding. Bind qualified information-confirmed events to the existing grounded-understanding source, not a new alias: participant is the performing living actor; require completed paid observations, valid evidence and genuinely new information. Use its existing 0.8 amount, cap 1, eight-round duration, refresh repetition and 12-round cooldown. Its maintained component gains 0.035 on qualifying participation and decays 0.0015 per round under the existing source's bounded saturation rules; do not reset its accumulated state or bypass its cap. Repeated known results, unsupported certificates, requesting, implementation and learning give no award. Do not add a separate mastery or calibration-completion reward. Physical effort, damage, hunger and survival remain governed independently by actual state.",
      "visualReview": "Show the real specimens and paid contact actions, progressive marks, transferred powder, fractured surfaces and conserved debris at their actual positions. Bind progress, completion, cancellation and invalidation displays to the declared contact-calibration events. Replay records must include specimen identities, stage, paid energy, remaining work, achieved geometry and force, observed alterations, model lineage and resulting bounds. Present relative evidence separately from absolute evidence; render unresolved bounds explicitly and never display a certified-tool badge before a valid assessment. Certificates are informational overlays, not newly created physical standards."
      ,
      "learning": 5
    }
  ]
}
